{
  "title": "72: Al-Jinn الجن",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقُلْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ اَنَّهُ اسْتَمَعَ نَفَرٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ فَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا سَمِعْنَا قُرْاٰنًاعَجَبًا ۙ‏(1)\nQUL OOHEYA ELAYYA ANNAHUS TAMA-A’ NAFARUM MENAL JINNE FA-QAALOO INNAA SAME’NAA QUR-AANAN A’JABAA.\nSay, ‘It has been revealed to me that a team of the jinn listened [to the Quran] and they said, “Indeed we heard a wonderful Quran,\nيَّهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الرُّشْدِ فَاٰمَنَّا بِهٖ‌ ؕ وَلَنْ نُّشْرِكَ بِرَبِّنَاۤ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(2)\nYAHDEE ELAR RUSHDE FA-AAMANNAA BEH, WA LAN NUSHREKA BE-RABBENAA AHADAA.\nwhich guides to rectitude. Hence, we have believed in it and we will never ascribe any partner to our Lord.\nوَّاَنَّهٗ تَعٰلٰى جَدُّ رَبِّنَا مَا اتَّخَذَ صَاحِبَةً وَّلَا وَلَدًا ۙ‏(3)\nWA ANNAHU TA-A’ALAA JADDO RABBENAA MAT TAKHAZA SAAHEBATANW WA LAA WALADAA.\nExalted be the majesty of our Lord; He has taken neither any spouse nor son.\nوَّ اَنَّهٗ كَانَ يَقُوْلُ سَفِيْهُنَا عَلَى اللّٰهِ شَطَطًا ۙ‏(4)\nWA ANNAHU KAANA YAQOOLO SAFEEHONAA A’LAL LAAHE SHATATAA.\nThe foolish ones among us used to speak atrocious lies concerning Allah.\nوَّاَنَّا ظَنَنَّاۤ اَنْ لَّنْ تَقُوْلَ الْاِنْسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا ۙ‏(5)\nWA ANNAA ZANANNAA AL LAN TAQOOLAL INSO WAL JINNO A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAA.\nWe thought that humans and jinn would never utter any falsehood concerning Allah.\nوَّاَنَّهٗ كَانَ رِجَالٌ مِّنَ الْاِنْسِ يَعُوْذُوْنَ بِرِجَالٍ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ فَزَادُوْهُمْ رَهَقًا ۙ‏(6)\nWA ANNAHU KAANA REJAALUM MENAL INSE YA-O’OZOONA BE-REJAALIM MENAL JINNE FA-ZAADOOHUM RAHAQAA.\nIndeed some persons from the humans would seek the protection of some persons from the jinn, thus only adding to their rebellion.\nوَّاَنَّهُمْ ظَنُّوْا كَمَا ظَنَنْتُمْ اَنْ لَّنْ يَّبْعَثَ اللّٰهُ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(7)\nWA ANNAHUM ZANNOO KAMAA ZANANTUM AL LAN-Y YAB-A’SAL LAAHO AHADAA.\nThey thought, just as you think, that Allah will not raise anyone from the dead.\nوَّاَنَّا لَمَسْنَا السَّمَآءَ فَوَجَدْنٰهَا مُلِئَتْ حَرَسًا شَدِيْدًا وَّشُهُبًا ۙ‏(8)\nWA ANNAA LAMASNAS SAMAAA-A FA-WAJADNAAHAA MOLE-AT HARASAN SHADEEDANW WA SHOHOBAA.\nIndeed we made for the heaven and found it full of mighty sentries and flames.\nوَّاَنَّا كُنَّا نَقْعُدُ مِنْهَا مَقَاعِدَ لِلسَّمْعِ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ يَّسْتَمِعِ الْاٰنَ يَجِدْ لَهٗ شِهَابًا رَّصَدًا ۙ‏(9)\nWA ANNAA KUNNAA NAQ-O’DO MINHAA MAQAA-E’DA LIS-SAM’, FAMAN-Y YASTAME-I’L AANA YAJID LAHU SHEHAABAR RASADAA.\nWe used to sit in its positions to eavesdrop, but anyone listening now finds a flame waiting for him.\nوَّاَنَّا لَا نَدْرِىْۤ اَشَرٌّ اُرِيْدَ بِمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَمْ اَرَادَ بِهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ رَشَدًا ۙ‏(10)\nWA ANNAA LAA NADREE ASHARRUN OREEDA BEMAN FIL ARZE AM ARAADA BEHIM RABBOHUM RASHADAA.\nWe do not know whether ill is intended for those who are on the earth, or whether their Lord intends good for them.\nوَّاَنَّا مِنَّا الصّٰلِحُوْنَ وَمِنَّا دُوْنَ ذٰلِكَ‌ؕ كُنَّا طَرَآئِقَ قِدَدًا ۙ‏(11)\nWA ANNAA MINNAS SAALEHOONA WA MINNAA DOONA ZAALEK, KUNNAA TARAAA-EQA QEDADAA.\nAmong us some are righteous and some are otherwise: we are various sects.\nوَّاَنَّا ظَنَنَّاۤ اَنْ لَّنْ نُّعْجِزَ اللّٰهَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَنْ نُّعْجِزَهٗ هَرَبًا ۙ‏(12)\nWA ANNAA ZANANNAA AL LAN NO’JEZAL LAAHA FIL ARZE WA LAN NO’JEZAHU HARABAA.\nWe know that we cannot frustrate Allah on the earth, nor can we frustrate Him by fleeing.\nوَّاَنَّا لَمَّا سَمِعْنَا الْهُدٰٓى اٰمَنَّا بِهٖ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ يُّؤْمِنْۢ بِرَبِّهٖ فَلَا يَخَافُ بَخْسًا وَّلَا رَهَقًا ۙ‏(13)\nWA ANNAA LAMMAA SAME’NAL HODAA AAMANNAA BEH, FAMAN-Y YOAMIM BE-RABBEHI FALAA YAKHAAFO BAKHSANW WA LAA RAHAQAA.\nWhen we heard the [message of] guidance, we believed in it. Whoever that has faith in his Lord will fear neither privation nor oppression.\nوَّاَنَّا مِنَّا الْمُسْلِمُوْنَ وَمِنَّا الْقٰسِطُوْنَ‌ؕ فَمَنْ اَسْلَمَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ تَحَرَّوْا رَشَدًا‏(14)\nWA ANNAA MINNAL MUSLEMOONA WA MINNAL QAASETOON, FAMAN ASLAMA FA-OOLAAA-EKA TAHARRAW RASHADAA.\nAmong us some are Muslims and some of us are perverse.” ’ Those who submit [to Allah]—it is they who pursue rectitude.\nوَاَمَّا الْقٰسِطُوْنَ فَكَانُوْا لِجَهَنَّمَ حَطَبًا ۙ‏(15)\nWA AMMAL QAASETOONA FA-KAANOO LE-JAHANNAMA HATABAA.\nAs for the perverse, they will be firewood for hell.\nوَّاَنْ لَّوِ اسْتَقَامُوْا عَلَى الطَّرِيْقَةِ لَاَسْقَيْنٰهُمْ مَّآءً غَدَقًا ۙ‏(16)\nWA ALLAWIS TAQAAMOO A’LAT TAREEQATE LA-ASQAYNAAHUM MAAA-AN GHADAQAA.\nIf they are steadfast on the path [of Allah], We shall provide them with abundant water,\nلِّنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّعْرِضْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ رَبِّهٖ يَسْلُكْهُ عَذَابًا صَعَدًا ۙ‏(17)\nLE-NAFTENAHUM FEEH, WA MAN-Y YO’RIZ A’N ZIKRE RABBEHI YASLUKHO A’ZAABAN SA-A’DAA.\nso that We may test them therein, and whoever turns away from the remembrance of his Lord, He will let him into an escalating punishment.\nوَّاَنَّ الْمَسٰجِدَ لِلّٰهِ فَلَا تَدْعُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(18)\nWA ANNAL MASAAJEDA LILLAAHE FALAA TAD-O’O MA-A’L LAAHE AHADAA.\nThe places of worship belong to Allah, so do not invoke anyone along with Allah.\nوَّاَنَّهٗ لَمَّا قَامَ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ يَدْعُوْهُ كَادُوْا يَكُوْنُوْنَ عَلَيْهِ لِبَدًا ؕ‏(19)\nWA ANNAHU LAMMAA QAAMA A’BDUL LAAHE YAD-O’OHO KAADOO YAKOONOONA A’LAYHE LEBADAA.\nWhen the servant of Allah rose to pray to Him, they almost crowded around him.\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَدْعُوْا رَبِّىْ وَلَاۤ اُشْرِكُ بِهٖۤ اَحَدًا‏(20)\nQUL INNAMAA AD-O’O RABBEE WA LAA USHREKO BEHI AHADAA.\nSay, ‘I pray only to my Lord, and I do not ascribe any partner to Him.’\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ لَاۤ اَمْلِكُ لَكُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا رَشَدًا‏(21)\nQUL INNEE LAA AMLEKO LAKUM ZARRANW WA LAA RASHADAA.\nSay, ‘I have no power to bring you any harm or good [of my own accord].’\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ لَنْ يُّجِيْرَنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اَحَدٌ  ۙ وَّلَنْ اَجِدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مُلْتَحَدًا ۙ‏(22)\nQUL INNEE LAN-Y YOJEERANEE MENAL LAAHE AHADUNW, WA LAN AJEDA MIN DOONEHI MULTAHADAA.\nSay, ‘Neither can anyone shelter me from Allah, nor can I find any refuge besides Him.\nاِلَّا بَلٰغًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرِسٰلٰتِهٖ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّعْصِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاِنَّ لَهٗ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ‏(23)\nILLAA BALAAGHAM MENAL LAAHE WA RESAALAATEH, WA MAN-Y YA’SIL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA-INNA LAHU NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAA.\n[I have no duty] except to transmit from Allah, and [to communicate] His messages; and whoever disobeys Allah and His apostle, there will indeed be for him the fire of hell, to remain in it forever.’\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا رَاَوْا مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَ فَسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ اَضْعَفُ نَاصِرًا وَّاَقَلُّ عَدَدًا‏(24)\nHATTAA EZAA RA-AW MAA YOO-A’DOONA FASAYA’LAMOONA MAN AZ-A’FO NAASERANW WA AQALLO A’DADAA.\nWhen they see what they are promised, they will know who is weaker in supporters and fewer in numbers.\nقُلْ اِنْ اَدْرِىْۤ اَقَرِيْبٌ مَّا تُوْعَدُوْنَ اَمْ يَجْعَلُ لَهٗ رَبِّىْۤ اَمَدًا‏(25)\nQUL IN ADREE AQAREEBUM MAA TOO-A’DOONA AM YAJ-A’LO LAHU RABBEE AMADAA.\nSay, ‘I do not know if what you are promised is near, or if my Lord has set a [long] term for it.’\nعٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ فَلَا يُظْهِرُ عَلٰى غَيْبِهٖۤ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(26)\nA’ALEMUL GHAYBE FALAA YUZHERO A’LAA GHAYBEHI AHADAA.\nKnower of the Unseen, He does not disclose His [knowledge of the] Unseen to anyone,\nاِلَّا مَنِ ارْتَضٰى مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ فَاِنَّهٗ يَسْلُكُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهٖ رَصَدًا ۙ‏(27)\nILLAA MANIR TAZAA MIR RASOOLIN FA-INNAHU YASLOKO MIM BAYNE YADAYHE WA MIN KHALFEHI RASADAA.\nexcept to an apostle He approves of. Then He dispatches a sentinel before and behind him\nلِّيَعْلَمَ اَنْ قَدْ اَبْلَغُوْا رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَاَحَاطَ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ وَاَحْصٰى كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عَدَدًا‏(28)\nLE-YA’LAMA AN QAD ABLAGHOO RESAALAATE RABBEHIM WA AHAATA BEMAA LADAYHIM WA AHSAA KULLA SHAY-IN A’DADAA.\nso that He may ascertain that they have communicated the messages of their Lord, and He encompasses all that is with them, and He keeps an count of all things.",
  "merits": "This ‘Makki’ Surah has 28 verses. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that frequent recitation of this Surah is a protection from Jinn and the reciter will be in the company of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) on the Day of Resurrection. This Surah also protects one from the evil actions of an unjust person.\nPrisoners secure early release by reciting this Surah and those who recite it properly will never face poverty or starvation. Keeping this Surah in one’s possession ensures safety from the Jinn, victory in debate or confrontation, and safety of possession and wealth. Debts are also easily paid back."
}
